          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: справедливый",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "справедливый (spravedlívyy) — \"fair, even-handed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Наш учитель строгий, но справедливый. Nash uchítel strógiy, no spravedlívyy. Our teacher is strict but fair."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Справедливо — fairly, or it is fair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "справедливый (spravedlívyy) is usually traced to the root of правда \"truth\" and право \"right\", Proto-Slavic pravŭ \"right, correct\" (EtymDB), through a Church Slavonic formation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
